  "goodToKnow": "Der Kosmos is the cosmos or universe: die Entstehung des Kosmos. Figuratively, it's a self-contained world: der Kosmos einer Kleinstadt. Alexander von Humboldt's five-volume Kosmos (1845–1862) tried to describe the entire physical world and was a bestseller. Kosmisch means cosmic, and der Kosmonaut a Soviet or Russian astronaut. From Greek kosmos (order, world). It has no plural in normal use."
